# github-projects (Cursor)

One board can contain more than one PB. Board is source of truth.
README is contract. Issue is execution unit for AI and human.

## Clarify first (mandatory)

Do NOT create board or issues if any is missing. Ask until complete:
PB list + titles, Owner + author (written by name/date),
affected repos + work branch + base per PB,
wave plan (W0 foundation, W1 backend, W2 frontend, W3 QA/deploy),
per issue Definition, Changes, Success (Test mandatory), Dependencies.
Do not guess.

## README multi-PB

Header (Owner, Written by, Status), PB list table,
How We Work (waves), Affected Repos table (Repo, Used by PB, Branch, Base),
detail section per PB, decisions, open questions.
See `references/template-readme.md`.

## Issue 3-scope

1. Definition + out-of-scope.
2. Changes + repo/branch.
3. Success: Functional + Test (command + evidence, mandatory) + Regression.
Header: `Wave: Wx | Repo: | Branch: | Depends: | Blocks:`.
No Test block = NOT Ready. See `references/template-issue.md`.

## Waves + dependencies

Waves sequential, parallel inside one wave allowed.
If Depends is not Done, issue stays Todo/Backlog.
Use waves for large features. See `references/views.md` for views.

## Views

Create manually (no CLI for views):
All Work Items (table), Engineering Workflow (board by Status),
Delivery Roadmap (roadmap), Development Sequence
(table, filter `-delivery-stage:Tracking`, sort Delivery Stage then Target Date).
